@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Cookie Policy";
    ViewData["Description"] = "How the Palm Engineering website uses cookies and browser storage.";
}

@section Hero {
    <div class="page-banner">
        <div class="page-banner-inner">
            <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">Cookie Policy</li></ol></nav>
            <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
        </div>
    </div>
}

<div class="container">
<article class="legal">
    <p class="updated">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-11-18">18 November 2026</time></p>

    <p>
        This policy explains how the @Biz.TradingName website ("@Biz.LegalName") uses cookies and similar technologies.
        It should be read with our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>1. What are cookies?</h2>
    <p>
        Cookies are small text files that a website saves on your device. Similar technologies, such as your browser's
        local storage, can also keep small pieces of information on your device.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What we use</h2>
    <p><strong>Cookies:</strong> this website does not set any cookies. We do not use analytics, advertising or tracking cookies.</p>
    <p><strong>Local storage:</strong> we use your browser's local storage for two small, optional features. Neither is sent to us.</p>

    <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
    <table class="policy-table">
        <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Lasts</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>palm.shortlist.v1</code></td><td>Remembers the gallery items you choose to save, so they are still there when you return.</td><td>Local storage, first party, strictly functional</td><td>Until you clear it</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>palm.cookie-notice.v1</code></td><td>Remembers that you have seen the cookie notice so we do not show it again.</td><td>Local storage, first party, strictly functional</td><td>Until you clear it</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>

    <h2>3. Third parties</h2>
    <p>
        This website loads no third-party scripts, fonts, maps, videos or social media widgets, so no third party
        can set cookies through it. If we link to another website, that site's own policy applies once you leave ours.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Consent</h2>
    <p>
        Because we only use storage that is needed for features you ask for, we do not need your consent and there is
        nothing to switch off. If we ever add analytics, advertising or other non-essential cookies, we will update this
        policy and ask for your consent first.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Managing or deleting stored data</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Use <strong>Clear</strong> in the gallery shortlist to remove saved items.</li>
        <li>Clear this site's data in your browser settings (usually under Privacy or Site settings).</li>
        <li>Most browsers let you block or delete cookies and site data at any time. Blocking local storage will not stop the website working, but your shortlist will not be remembered.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy? Email <a href="mailto:@Biz.Email">@Biz.Email</a>.</p>
</article>
</div>
